      "name": "SetBackBufferHeightFromScreenWidth",
      "signature": "void SetBackBufferHeightFromScreenWidth(void)",
      "calling_convention": "__stdcall",
      "return_type": "void",
      "comment": "Copies screen width to back buffer height global.\n\nClassification: Leaf function / Initialization helper\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Load current screen width from g_dwScreenWidth (0x6fbae0e4)\n2. Store value to g_dwBackBufferHeight (0x6fbdc014)\n3. Return\n\nParameters: None\n\nReturns: void\n\nCalled Context:\n- Referenced from function pointer table at 0x6fbae004\n- Used during graphics mode initialization/reconfiguration\n\nGlobal Variables:\n- g_dwScreenWidth (0x6fbae0e4) [READ] - Current screen width in pixels\n- g_dwBackBufferHeight (0x6fbdc014) [WRITE] - Back buffer height dimension\n\nNote: This function sets back buffer height equal to screen width, which may be\nused for square aspect ratio rendering or rotation scenarios.",
