      "name": "ScanStringWithFormat",
      "signature": "int ScanStringWithFormat(char * szInput, byte * pbFormat)",
      "calling_convention": "__cdecl",
      "return_type": "int",
      "comment": "Scans an input string using a scanf-style format specifier.\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Initialize scan context with type 0x49 ('I' = input)\n2. Store input string pointer for start and current position\n3. Calculate input string length via strlen\n4. Call internal scanf parser (FUN_6ff7832c) with context and format\n\nParameters:\n- szInput (char*): Input string to scan/parse\n- pbFormat (byte*): Format specifier string (e.g. \"%d.%d.%d.%d\")\n\nReturns:\n- Number of successfully matched format specifiers\n\nMagic Numbers:\n- 0x49: Context type identifier ('I' = input mode)\n\nRelated Functions:\n- FUN_6ff7832c: Core scanf parser that performs actual pattern matching",
