      "name": "DispatchJumpTableEntry",
      "signature": "void DispatchJumpTableEntry(int * piTargetData, void * pfnDispatchEntry)",
      "calling_convention": "__stdcall",
      "return_type": "void",
      "comment": "Jump table thunk that dispatches control to a function pointer entry via stack exchange.\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Pop return address into EAX\n2. Pop register parameter into ECX\n3. Exchange EAX with [ESP] to swap return address and target data\n4. Jump to EAX (which now contains function pointer)\n\nParameters:\n- piTargetData: int* - Target data/state passed via stack, swapped to EAX before dispatch\n- pfnDispatchEntry: void* - Function pointer address to dispatch to (passed via jump table)\n\nReturns:\n- No return: Control transferred to pfnDispatchEntry\n- Function pointer receives piTargetData in EAX via stack manipulation\n\nSpecial Cases:\n- Stack state manipulated via XCHG to pass parameter via EAX\n- Used within structured exception handling (ExceptionList setup by caller)\n- Jump table unrecoverable due to indirect dispatch mechanism\n\nMagic Numbers Reference:\n- 0x6fb99d3f: Function entry point\n- 0x6fb99d44: JMP instruction target (EAX)\n\nRelated Functions:\n- FUN_6fb9be4d() - Primary caller that validates conditions before dispatch\n- FUN_6fb9c011() - Secondary caller that acquires jump table entry",
      "name_source": "LoD/1.07",
      "method": "MNE",
