      "name": "CheckBindingStateFlagSet",
      "signature": "dword CheckBindingStateFlagSet(void * this, uint param_1)",
      "calling_convention": "__thiscall",
      "return_type": "dword",
      "comment": "Check if binding state flag 0x4 is set for given state index.\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Compare g_dwBindingMode with 2\n2. If binding mode < 2:\n   - Load byte from g_pBindingStates[nStateIndex * 2]\n   - Mask with 0x4 to check flag bit\n3. Otherwise:\n   - Call FUN_6fb9f44c with this, nStateIndex, and 0x4 flag\n4. If flag not set (dwFlagValue == 0):\n   - Clear bit 0x20 (AND 0xFFFFFFDF)\n   - Subtract 7\n5. Return modified state index\n\nParameters:\n- this (IMPLICIT in ECX): Object pointer\n- nStateIndex (uint): State/slot index to check\n\nReturns:\n- Modified state index value; flag cleared if not set",
      "name_source": "LoD/1.07",
