      "name": "ReadByteFromBuffer",
      "signature": "byte ReadByteFromBuffer(dword * pdwState)",
      "calling_convention": "__cdecl",
      "return_type": "byte",
      "comment": "Reads next byte from buffer and manages state counter.\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Load state pointer (contains buffer position and remaining count)\n2. Decrement count at state+0x4\n3. If count >= 0: load byte from buffer at state[0], increment buffer pointer, return byte\n4. If count < 0: call refill function FUN_6fb9e41c to load more data, return result\n\nParameters:\n- pdwState (dword *): Pointer to state structure with [0]=buffer_ptr, [4]=count\n\nReturns:\n- Byte value from buffer (0-255)\n- Result from FUN_6fb9e41c if count exhausted\n\nSpecial Cases:\n- Negative count (-1 or less) triggers refill before returning next byte\n- Buffer pointer auto-incremented after each byte read\n- Note: Function uses SSA temporaries optimized away by decompiler",
      "name_source": "LoD/1.07",
      "method": "MNE",
