      "name": "ProcessExceptionFrameRestoration",
      "signature": "void ProcessExceptionFrameRestoration(int nExcRecord, int nFrameDataOffset, byte * pbFrameData, byte * pbRestoreBuffer)",
      "calling_convention": "__cdecl",
      "return_type": "void",
      "comment": "Processes exception frame restoration by conditionally copying frame data or restoring exception state.\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Validate frame data: Check pbFrameData[4] non-null, pbFrameData[8] non-null\n2. Calculate target address: piTargetData = pbFrameData[8+0xC] + nFrameDataOffset\n3. Initialize dwState to zero\n4. Check pbFrameData[0] bit 3 (0x08)\n5. Branch on pbRestoreBuffer[0] bit 0 (0x01)\n6. Check pbRestoreBuffer[0x18] for handler vs data mode\n7. Validate with FUN_6fba14c8, FUN_6fba14e4\n8. Copy data or dispatch based on flags\n9. Call FUN_6fb9c2d9 if validation fails\n10. Restore ExceptionList and return\n\nParameters:\nnExcRecord - Exception record address\nnFrameDataOffset - Frame data offset for target calculation\npbFrameData - Frame data buffer\npbRestoreBuffer - Restoration/processing buffer\n\nReturns:\nvoid - Always returns, restores exception context\n\nSpecial Cases:\nNote: Function uses 9 compiler-optimized phantom variables (extraout_var_*) that cannot be renamed",
