      "name": "InsertStringSpace",
      "signature": "void InsertStringSpace(char * lpszBuffer, int nSpaceCount)",
      "calling_convention": "__cdecl",
      "return_type": "void",
      "comment": "Creates space in a string by shifting existing content to the right.\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Check if space count is non-zero; return early if zero\n2. Calculate the current length of the null-terminated string using strlen\n3. Use memory move operation to shift existing content (including null terminator) to the right by nSpaceCount positions\n4. The resulting string has nSpaceCount empty characters at position nSpaceCount from the original start\n\nParameters:\nlpszBuffer (char*): Null-terminated string buffer to modify (must have sufficient capacity for expansion)\nnSpaceCount (int): Number of character positions to insert at the beginning\n\nReturns:\nvoid: Function modifies the input buffer in-place\n\nSpecial Cases:\nIf nSpaceCount is 0, function returns without modification\nBuffer must have adequate capacity to accommodate the expanded string\nOriginal content is preserved and moved to positions [nSpaceCount..length+nSpaceCount]\n\nMagic Numbers Reference:\n0x01: Increment to include null terminator in memory move operation",
      "name_source": "LoD/1.07",
      "method": "CAL",
      "index": "CAL:ea3677ef9e925b399045d64b19f6ab3e",
