      "name": "ProcessStreamDataWithLineEnding",
      "signature": "int ProcessStreamDataWithLineEnding(uint dwFileIndex, char * lpszBuffer, uint dwMaxBytes)",
      "calling_convention": "__cdecl",
      "return_type": "int",
      "comment": "Reads from file handle with text-mode line ending conversion.\n\nConverts Windows CR/LF line endings to Unix LF and detects Ctrl-Z EOF.\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Validate buffer pointer not NULL, check file handle entry flags\n2. If buffered mode (0x48) and pending lookahead char present, prepend it\n3. Call Windows ReadFile API to read raw bytes into buffer\n4. On error: map errno 5 to EBADF(9) and return -1; for 0x6d return 0\n5. If text mode (0x80 flag) is set, process line ending conversion:\n   a. Skip CR if followed by LF (convert CR/LF to LF)\n   b. Handle Ctrl-Z (0x1A) as EOF marker with flag 0x40 check\n   c. For edge cases at buffer boundary, read one lookahead byte\n\nParameters:\n- dwFileIndex (uint): File handle index into g_ppFileHandleTable array\n- lpszBuffer (char*): Destination buffer for read data output\n- dwMaxBytes (uint): Maximum bytes to read into buffer\n\nReturns:\n- Bytes read on success (may be less than dwMaxBytes)\n- 0 on EOF or null buffer or ERROR_BROKEN_PIPE\n- -1 on read error with errno set\n\nMagic Numbers:\n- 0x24 (36): File handle structure stride in bytes\n- 0x1F (31): Handle index mask for lower 5 bits\n- 0x48: Buffered mode flags (lookahead enabled)\n- 0x80: Text mode flag (convert CR/LF to LF)\n- 0x1A (26): Ctrl-Z EOF marker character\n- 0x6D (109): ERROR_BROKEN_PIPE Windows error code",
      "name_source": "LoD/1.07",
