      "name": "ExecuteCatchHandlerBlock",
      "signature": "void * ExecuteCatchHandlerBlock(EHExceptionRecord * pExceptionRecord, EHRegistrationNode * pRegistrationNode, _CONTEXT * pContext, _s_FuncInfo * pFuncInfo, void * pCatchObject, int nContinuationAddress, ulong dwFlags)",
      "calling_convention": "__cdecl",
      "return_type": "void *",
      "comment": "Execute a C++ exception handler catch block within a try-except structure.\n\nThis is a Visual Studio C++ Runtime (MSVCRT) exception handling function that manages the execution of catch block handlers. It saves and restores exception context, creates frame information for stack unwinding, and invokes the appropriate catch handler based on exception type matching.\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Initialize SEH (Structured Exception Handling) prologue with 0x40 size and g_dwSEHPrologData marker\n2. Save current exception handler context by storing pointer to EBX in stack frame\n3. Load registration node exception offset and create FrameInfo structure for stack frame\n4. Save current _unexpected and _translator thread-local handlers\n5. Install new exception handlers: set _unexpected to pExceptionRecord, _translator to pContext\n6. Set sehState flag to 1 (active exception handling in progress)\n7. Call _CallCatchBlock2 with registration node, function info, and catch parameters\n8. Restore sehState to 0xffffffff after handler execution\n9. Invoke CleanupExceptionUnwind to restore exception context\n10. Return result from _CallCatchBlock2 (catch handler return value or void*)\n\nParameters:\npExceptionRecord: EHExceptionRecord* - Exception information including type, severity, and parameters\npRegistrationNode: EHRegistrationNode* - Exception handling registration node with frame linkage\npContext: _CONTEXT* - Processor context at exception point (EIP, registers, stack state)\npFuncInfo: _s_FuncInfo* - Function information including catch handler table and frame layout\npCatchObject: void* - Catch parameter/exception object passed to handler\ncontinuationAddress: int - Return address for handler continuation (EIP in CONTEXT)\nflags: ulong - Exception handling flags and options\n\nReturns:\nvoid* - Return value from catch handler execution, or nullptr if no handler matched\n\nSpecial Cases:\n- Exception signature 0xe06d7363 indicates Microsoft C++ exception format\n- Catch handlers matched by type checking: version field at offset +0x10 must equal 3\n- Type codes 0x19930520 and 0x19930521 indicate managed/native exception types\n- Field at offset +0x1c controls handler continuation (0 = match found and execute)\n- SEH state transitions: initialized (1) -> cleanup (-1) for exception unwinding\n- If no catch handler matches, function returns 0x0 (false) from validation\n- Thread-local handler pointers are saved/restored to support nested exception contexts\n- FrameInfo structure cached on stack at [EBP - 0x50] for unwind information",
      "name_source": "LoD/1.11",
