      "comment": "C++ Exception Stack Unwinding Cleanup Handler\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Save exception dispatch pointer from [EBP-0x38] to [EDI-4]\n2. Unlink and cleanup frame info structure via _FindAndUnlinkFrame\n3. Retrieve thread-local data via __getptd()\n4. Restore exception translator callback from [EBP-0x40] to thread state at offset +0x7c\n5. Restore unexpected exception handler from [EBP-0x44] to thread state at offset +0x80\n6. Validate exception object signature (must equal 0xe06d7363 = MSVC \"msc\" marker)\n7. Validate exception type field at offset +0x10 (must equal 3 for C++ exception)\n8. Validate exception marker at offset +0x14 (must be 0x19930520 or 0x19930521)\n9. Check rethrow flag at [EBP-0x48] (must be 0 to allow destruction)\n10. Check catcher flag at [EBP-0x20] (must be nonzero = handler exists)\n11. If all conditions met, check IsExceptionObjectToBeDestroyed([ESI+0x18])\n12. If should destroy, call __abnormal_termination() and ___DestructExceptionObject([ESI])\n13. Return to CallCatchBlock dispatcher\n\nParameters:\n  EBP: Stack frame base pointer (caller-provided frame pointer for exception context)\n  ESI: Exception object pointer to MSVC throw object with internal metadata structure\n  EDI: Dispatch table entry for exception handler resumption and control flow\n  [EBP-0x38]: Exception dispatch pointer to restore to stack frame\n  [EBP-0x3c]: FrameInfo structure pointer for unwinding chain management\n  [EBP-0x40]: Exception translator callback to restore to thread state\n  [EBP-0x44]: Unexpected exception handler to restore to thread state\n  [EBP-0x48]: Rethrow flag (0=can destroy object, nonzero=rethrow in progress)\n  [EBP-0x20]: Catcher exists flag (0=no handler, nonzero=has catch block)\n\nReturns:\n  void: Returns control to exception dispatcher via RET instruction\n\nSpecial Cases:\n  - Magic signature 0xe06d7363: MSVC C++ exception marker (ASCII \"msc\")\n  - Exception marker 0x19930520: Visual C++ 5.x - 6.x exception type identifier\n  - Exception marker 0x19930521: Visual C++ exception type identifier (variant)\n  - Destruction only occurs if ALL validation checks pass AND rethrow is false\n  - Unaffected registers (EBP, ESI, EDI) are callee-saved per calling convention\n\nException Object Structure (ESI):\n  Offset | Size | Field       | Type    | Description\n  -------|------|-------------|---------|------------------------------------------------\n  +0x00  | 4    | dwSignature | DWORD   | 0xe06d7363 (MSVC marker)\n  +0x10  | 4    | dwType      | DWORD   | Exception type code (must be 3)\n  +0x14  | 4    | dwMarker    | DWORD   | Version marker (0x19930520/0x19930521)\n  +0x18  | 4    | pfnDestr    | DWORD   | Function pointer to exception destructor\n  +0x1c  | var  | ExData      | Data    | Type-specific exception information",
