      "comment": "Initialize global audio stream frame node and register cleanup handler\n\nPurpose:\nThis function is called during program/DLL initialization to set up critical\nglobal data structures and ensure proper cleanup at program exit. It initializes\nthe global audio stream frame node structure and registers a cleanup function\nto be executed via atexit() when the program terminates.\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Call InitializeExceptionHandler() with pointer to global audio stream frame\n   node structure (g_pAudioStreamFrameNode at 0x6fc45870)\n   - This function initializes the frame node and sets up linked list pointers\n2. Register ClearDataStructure (at 0x6fc327c0) as cleanup callback via _atexit()\n   - This ensures the cleanup function is called during program exit sequence\n3. Return to caller\n\nParameters:\nNone - This is an initialization function called from program entry point\n\nReturns:\nvoid - No return value\n\nSpecial Cases:\n- Global data structure address is fixed at 0x6fc45870 (g_pAudioStreamFrameNode)\n- Cleanup function at 0x6fc327c0 must be registered before any audio processing\n- This must be called exactly once during initialization, typically from\n  DLL_PROCESS_ATTACH or equivalent entry point\n- The structure is a linked list of audio stream frame nodes with pointers to\n  data blocks and stream metadata\n\nCross-references:\n- Called from: 0x6fc4000c (data reference in function pointer table)\n- Calls: InitializeExceptionHandler (0x6fbf44d0), _atexit (0x6fbf5937)\n- Cleanup handler: ClearDataStructure (0x6fc327c0)",
